{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/816333-leaving-the-lair","id":816333,"title":"Leaving the Lair","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T12:17:17-08:00","id":816333,"title":"Leaving the Lair","content":"If your Lair is connected to the local Hive, your Horror gets access to a much larger hunting ground, right? As far as I can tell, it can straight up leave the Lair travel the Hive. Is this correct? If I am controlling my Horror with instant actions, can I use my Horror to leave the Lair and explore the Hive and, for example, see where all the other Lairs connected to the Hive are? Or go find some poor dreaming mortal to feed on?<br /> <br /> If I am controlling my Horror outside of my Lair (wandering the Hive with it), what happens if I open a Primordial Pathway to my Lair? Is the Horror gone? Do I have to guide it back to my Lair before I can merge with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:49:25-08:00","id":816540,"title":"","content":"Yes, Yes, I don't see why not, Definitely, and a hard call; you could play it one of three ways: either you merge and it takes an amount of narrative time for the Horror to return to the Lair, the Path can't be open (boring option, but has its uses), or my favourite, you have to track down the Horror within the Hive, much like having to rouse a Slumbering Horror, wherein you travel the Astral as a mundane human until you find the Horror and merge at the site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T18:11:03-08:00","id":816554,"title":"","content":"Huh. That could be fun. Though I assume that you could always just use instant actions to pilot the Horror back to you rather than having to go find it.<br /> <br /> Did we ever figure out if the Horror can open Primordial Pathways from its end? I want to say no, but it seems like it would have to be able to do so in order to travel to the dreamscapes of the mortals it feeds on. ... I suppose the better question is, can I, acting as my Horror with instant actions, use my Horror to open a Primordial Pathway? The reason I want to say that no, it can't, is that if it can, why would I bother trying to open them myself when I could just open them from the Horror's end and never suffer dice penalties for having the external end of the Pathway being somewhere that isn't the Lair?<br /> <br /> Well, that and because having the Horror open Primordial Pathways to the material world would also allow you to do things like assassinate someone with your Horror while your human body is sitting in a Starbucks a mile away, though YMMV as to whether that should be allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 01-25-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:04:04-08:00","id":816576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/816333-leaving-the-lair?p=816554#post816554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. That could be fun. Though I assume that you could always just use instant actions to pilot the Horror back to you rather than having to go find it.<br /> <br /> Did we ever figure out if the Horror open Primordial Pathways from its end? I want to say no, but it seems like it would have to be able to do so in order to travel to the dreamscapes of the mortals it feeds on. ... I suppose the better question is, can I, acting as my Horror with instant actions, use my Horror to open a Primordial Pathway? The reason I want to say that no, it can't, is that if it can, why would I bother trying to open them myself when I could just open them from the Horror's end and never suffer dice penalties for having the external end of the Pathway being somewhere that isn't the Lair?<br /> <br /> Well, that and because having the Horror open Primordial Pathways to the material world would also allow you to do things like assassinate someone with your Horror while your human body is sitting in a Starbucks a mile away, though YMMV as to whether that should be allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not into other realms, most likely, for some sensible, if a little convenient, reasons elucidated in Chapter 2. Basically, short of extreme narrative circumstances (vis-a-vis the Inheritance), the greater narrative reality of the fallen world cannot possibly accommodate the existence of a monster constructed entirely of reified fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}